{
  "name": "maintenance",
  "description": "The worn regime, end to end, on the Grinder. Opens with klapaucius (the flavour-line precedent: the subject is what a worn machine does, not the economy), buys kola nuts at the bin, and grinds batch after batch until wear (2 per operation) drops the cell below the effect threshold — at which point it runs at half speed, jams (9 whacked out by hand) and spoils inputs on the deterministic cadence (17 wasted). Ends with one $8 repair kit bought at the bin and spent standing by the machine — whole cell back to full in one use — and a short tail of the restored grinder back at work. Re-recorded 2026-08-27 after item 145 deleted the Chip Kitchen the previous recording ran on; see scripts/record-maintenance.ts.",
